===============================================================================
PART 4 AGAINST THE SEAM'S NEW SHAPE - the reconciliation that matters
===============================================================================
The order is right that two reset mechanisms on one seam is the two-owners shape,
and that this must compose rather than sit beside. Here is what they actually are,
verified rather than assumed.

Upstream's positive recovery reset - fm_failure_episode_reset - clears
  .turnend-claude-blocks, .claude-autoarm-failure-notified,
  .claude-autoarm-failure-alarmed
which is the CLAUDE STOP AUTO-ARM FAILURE EPISODE: how many times the turn-end
guard has blocked a stop, and whether the last-resort notice and attended
fail-open have been spent. Its trigger, at bin/fm-turnend-guard.sh:149 and
bin/fm-claude-stop-autoarm.sh:208, is fm_watcher_healthy - a verified live,
identity-matched watcher with a fresh beacon.

This lane's Part 4 reset clears
  .wedge-escalations-<key>, .stale-since-<key>
which is the PER-PANE WEDGE ESCALATION RATCHET: how many times one crewmate's
pane has escalated as possibly wedged. Its trigger is evidence that the lane
moved - rendered output, process-tree CPU, or live descendants.

CLASSIFICATION: COMPLEMENTARY, and NOT duplicates. Different state, different
alarms, different subjects (the home's supervision chain vs one crewmate's pane),
different evidence. Neither can clear the other's alarm and neither should.

THE FINDING THAT MATTERS MORE THAN THE CLASSIFICATION: upstream's reset already
embodies Part 4's principle. It fires on POSITIVE EVIDENCE of health and never on
elapsed time. So "evidence of health resets alarm state, never time" is not a new
idea this lane is introducing to the seam - it is an established property of the
seam that Part 4 extends to a second alarm. That is a much stronger footing than
"bolted beside", and it changes how Part 4 should be written: as the same rule
applied consistently, using the same vocabulary, not as a parallel invention.

One distinction to state precisely, because it is exactly where a careless
reading would break the constraint. fm_watcher_healthy includes a beacon FRESHNESS
requirement, which is an age comparison. That does not violate "never time".
Requiring recent positive evidence ("something proved alive lately") is the
opposite of a time-based amnesty ("it has been quiet a while, so clear the
alarm"). The forbidden shape is elapsed silence CAUSING a reset. Upstream requires
evidence and additionally requires it to be recent; Part 4 requires evidence and
compares two samples. Both are evidence-first. Part 4's prohibition stands
unchanged and upstream does not weaken it.

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE BUILD: Part 4 is rebuilt on the post-sync fm-watch.sh, still
scoped to the stale alarms only, and states its relationship to
fm_failure_episode_reset explicitly in docs/watcher-continuity.md so the seam has
one documented reset PRINCIPLE with two named, non-overlapping applications -
rather than two undocumented mechanisms a later reader would have to discover.

===============================================================================
STILL OWED FROM THE CANCELLED ROUND - unchanged by the sync
===============================================================================
Carried in carry-forward-2026-08-04.log beside this file; neither is affected by
anything upstream did.

1. busy-alarm-reset (ask-user, unresolved by the captain). health_evidence_reset
   fires unconditionally including at the busy-no-completed-turn sites that were
   deliberately scoped out, so that alarm resets every poll and can never
   escalate. Withholding the rendered hash blanks one component while cpu and
   children are still sampled, and a busy pane's CPU advances by definition.
   Its test is vacuous on exactly that property: the fake backend makes the
   evidence unreadable for an unrelated reason. Code and test both.
2. reclaim-failure-reported-as-live-peer (ask-user, unresolved). A failed reclaim
   returns the verdict meaning "a verified-live holder has it", so the watcher
   announces a peer it never verified - false certainty inside a three-outcome
   design whose point is that undecidable is first-class.
Plus three auto-fix findings, including the GNU-only ppid form that fabricates
children=1 on macOS instead of reporting unknown - a fabricated observation on
the exact evidence channel the captain specified must be real.

Guard-class mutation requirements are unchanged, both mirror directions included:
time-alone-resets and nothing-resets each still need their own fixture.

